Key Takeaways
Why This Matters: Persistent storage is crucial for production virtual machines because it ensures:

Data Durability: Your data survives VM restarts, migrations, and updates
Scalability: Storage can be dynamically provisioned and expanded as needed
Flexibility: Different storage classes can be used for different performance requirements
Backup and Recovery: Persistent volumes can be backed up and restored independently
Real-World Applications:

Database VMs: Ensuring database data persists across maintenance windows
Application Servers: Maintaining application state and configuration
Development Environments: Preserving development work across sessions
Enterprise Workloads: Meeting compliance and data retention requirements
This knowledge prepares you for managing production virtual machine workloads in OpenShift Virtualization environments, where reliable and persistent storage is essential for business continuity and data integrity.
